/* book Worked example 2: Q: A curved falling-rate stage was measured on a solid with ms/A = 25 kg/m². The rates R in kg/(m²·h) at X = 0.20, 0.16, 0.12, 0.08 and 0.06 are 1.50, 1.25, 0.95, 0.60 and 0.38. Find the time to dry from X = 0.20 to 0.06 by graphical integration.
   1. Tabulate 1/R: 0.667, 0.800, 1.053, 1.667 and 2.632 m²·h/kg.
   2. Trapezoid areas: 0.04 × (0.667 + 0.800)/2 = 0.0293; 0.04 × (0.800 + 1.053)/2 = 0.0371; 0.04 × (1.053 + 1.667)/2 = 0.0544; 0.02 × (1.667 + 2.632)/2 = 0.0430.
   3. Total area under the 1/R curve = 0.1638 m²·h/kg.
   4. t = (ms/A) × area = 25 × 0.1638 = 4.09 h.
   5. Check: a straight falling line through the origin from R = 1.50 at X = 0.20 would give 25 × (0.20/1.50) ln(0.20/0.06) = 4.01 h, close because the data lie near that line.
   Answer: The falling-rate time is about 4.1 h. */
