/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Dryers are grouped by how they handle solids.
   - Continuous dryers receive wet solid and deliver dry solid without stopping.
   - In through-circulation drying, air is pushed through a bed of granular solid held on a perforated tray or belt.
   - The water balance on the air gives the drying rate.
   - t is drying time in h; Ms is dry solid mass in kg; X1 and X2 are initial and final solid moistures in kg water/kg dry solid; mda is dry-air mass flow in kg dry air/h; Y1 and Y2 are inlet and outlet air humidities in kg water/kg dry air.
   - This assumes the solid surface stays wet.
   - Selection rules follow from the solid and the scale.
*/
