/* book Worked example: Q: A rotary dryer treats 1000 kg/h of wet solid at 25 % moisture (wet basis) and delivers it at 2 % moisture (wet basis). Air enters at Y = 0.010 kg water/kg dry air and leaves at Y = 0.035. The air mass velocity is 2.0 kg/(m²·s) and L/D = 6. Find the water evaporated, the dry air rate, the shell diameter and the shell length.
   1. Bone-dry solid: S = 1000 × (1 − 0.25) = 750 kg/h.
   2. Water in feed: W₁ = 1000 × 0.25 = 250 kg/h.
   3. Product is 98 % solid, so P = 750/0.98 = 765.3 kg/h and W₂ = 765.3 − 750 = 15.3 kg/h.
   4. Water evaporated: W = 250 − 15.3 = 234.7 kg/h ≈ 235 kg/h.
   5. Humidity rise: Y₂ − Y₁ = 0.035 − 0.010 = 0.025 kg water/kg dry air.
   6. Dry air rate: mₐ = 234.7/0.025 = 9388 kg dry air/h = 2.608 kg/s.
   7. Cross-section: A = 2.608/2.0 = 1.304 m².
   8. Diameter: D = √(4 × 1.304/π) = 1.288 m. Use 1.3 m.
   9. Length: L = 6 × 1.3 = 7.8 m.
   10. Heat for evaporation alone: Q = 234.7 × 2400 = 5.63 × 10⁵ kJ/h.
   Answer: Water evaporated 234.7 kg/h, dry air 9388 kg/h (2.61 kg/s), shell diameter 1.3 m, shell length 7.8 m. */
